    "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 2121 experienced an overall gross strengthening of GBP 2.9 million on prior years' provisions in 2020. This deterioration was primarily driven by adverse development on energy, fire and other damage to property, third party liability, and reinsurance acceptances. These strengthenings were partially offset by releases on motor (other), marine, aviation and transport, and pecuniary loss. The prior year movements were influenced by expected COVID-19 losses impacting both the 2018 and 2019 years of account, with the 2019 year also affected by legal rulings in Australia. Natural catastrophe events from prior years, including California wildfires, Hawaiian volcanic eruptions, Hurricanes Michael and Florence, and Typhoon Jebi in 2018, as well as Typhoons Hagibis and Faxai, Hurricane Dorian, Townsville flooding, and Australian bushfires in 2019, also contributed to the movements. Man-made losses such as the Hamptons fine art fire and Brazilian warehouse fire in 2018, and a Sydney office fire loss in 2019, also played a role, alongside political risks losses in both 2018 and 2019.",
